{"key":"ics/T0816","id":"T0816","name":"Device Restart/Shutdown","domain":"ics","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["inhibit-response-function"],"platforms":["None"],"environments":["ics-ot"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may forcibly restart or shutdown a device in an ICS environment to disrupt and potentially negatively impact physical processes. Methods of device restart and shutdown exist in some devices as built-in, standard functionalities. These functionalities can be executed using interactive device web interfaces, CLIs, and network protocol commands. Unexpected restart or shutdown of control system devices may prevent expected response…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T0816","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--25dfc8ad-bd73-4dfd-84a9-3c3d383f76e9","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.623Z","source_object_version":"1.1","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0038","name":"Application Log Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0038","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9c2fa0ae-7abc-485a-97f6-699e3b6cf9fa","page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"id":"DC0108","name":"Device Alarm","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0108","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9d56be63-3501-4dd3-bb5f-63c580833298","page":"telemetry/DC0108/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0078","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a7f22107-02e5-4982-9067-6625d4a1765a","page":"telemetry/DC0078/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0801","name":"Detection of Device Restart/Shutdown","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0801","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--194cb4dd-81ca-4e64-94e2-911fab1219f9","relations